    "turn_text": "Now your host Ken Brew on news radio 700 WLW. You know, when you're the utility player, you got to be ready. You know, when they say bat forth, bat forth, then they might want you to play second base one day and then the next day they want you in left field. That's what you got to be. Scott Sloan out today, they said yesterday, can you come in? I said, Coach, where do you need me? He said, we need you to bat at nine o'clock. Coach, that's fine. Where should I play in the field? They said, just watch the dugout, I'll send you signals. It's the day after election, slowly's out. He'll hopefully be back tomorrow. I am the aforementioned Ken Brew and it's over. The election season is over. Only to start again probably in the next 25-30 minutes. That's just the way it is anymore. Now with City Council on the shorter term plan 2, who knows? It just might be 24-7, 365. You just don't know. someone who had a very very good night on Tuesday night first out of the box today with us he is uh... our representative from district to once again in the u.s. congress he is brad wenstra who won last night uh... by a margin of uh... just about fifty thousand votes and he is spending some time on this day after election to talk with us here now on seven hundred wlw brad good morning and congratulations hey thanks",
