    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "Well a couple things and you mentioned Adam Schiff as I sit on intelligence committee and I assume that he would take over as a As the chair, but let's go back just a little bit to remember the last time just for the election within the Democratic Party for the leader, Tim Ryan got a third of the vote. Nancy Pelosi needs to get 218 votes. And I believe that what it looks like right now is they have 221 in the house. She's going to need to get virtually everyone to vote for her on the floor. And some of the people ran saying they weren't going to vote for Nancy Pelosi. So that's going to be interesting in and of itself just within the Democratic Party. But when it comes to Mr. Schiff, you know, this is a guy that I got along with very well, and I still get along with him, but I don't agree with the route that he has taken since Donald Trump won. He seemed to be a fine cooperative member on the intelligence committee until Donald Trump won, and then it became all about taking Donald Trump down. And then we found out that within the FBI and DOJ, there were people trying to do that as well. So it's going to be interesting to see how much he wants to investigate because some of the things that we have finally got our eyes on with for the intelligence committee members on the Democrats I haven't even gone to look at and that's a shame and so we're going to be held accountable but don't forget the Senate has their role too. So I think when it comes to some of that investigating or doing this and that It may be a little bit futile, but because on the other side, on the Senate side, I think they'll be looking at things a little bit differently.",
